-Synthetic fixture proposal (the address is RFC 5737 documentation space):
+## Response and errors
 
+See [DASHBOARD_INTEGRATION.md](DASHBOARD_INTEGRATION.md) for complete field semantics. `trusted` is citation/schema validation only. `dry_run` and `effect_scope` distinguish simulator state. `approval_status` is pending/approved/rejected independent of the execution status; `approved_by` contains the approving service user's immutable ID. Invalid AI analysis fields are null and citations empty.
+
+Errors are structured without payload/exception echo:
 ```json
-{"incident_id":"SZ-000042","action_type":"BLOCK_IP","target":"192.0.2.10","parameters":{},"playbook_id":"SZ-PB-001","ttl_minutes":60}
+{"detail":{"code":"approval_required"}}
 ```
 
-Approval/rejection accepts `{}` or `{"reason":"Reviewed evidence"}`. Execute/rollback accepts no body. `dry_run=true` must be displayed prominently in any dashboard integration; simulated SUCCESS is not live containment.
-
-Errors use `{"detail":{"code":"..."}}`. Common codes are authentication_required (401), role_not_permitted (403), DENIED_PROTECTED_TARGET (403), proposal_not_found (404), approval_required (409), proposal_expired (409), self_approval_forbidden (403), ALREADY_EXECUTED (409), execution_already_claimed (409), rollback_not_available (409), and dependency_unavailable (503). Request validation uses HTTP 422 with locations/types but no echoed input values.
