@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Conditional Core handoff — do not apply blindly
+
+**No main backend source or database change was made.** The current deployed Core was not available, so no missing endpoint is asserted as fact. Run the read-only preflight first. If existing responses satisfy [INTEGRATION.md](INTEGRATION.md), no mandatory Core change is needed for dry-run AI/SOAR integration.
+
+The old package's Core commit is historical only. Prefer adapting `CoreContractMapper` to a verified shape over changing an already-correct Core endpoint. Give this document to the main backend integration workstream only when the corresponding check actually fails.
+
+| Conditional gap | Exact minimal read-only change | Why |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Incident detail missing | authenticated `GET /v1/incidents/{id}` returning `id`/`incident_id`, `status`, `priority`, `title`/`summary`, optional primary `host_id`/`asset_id`, reason list | Context metadata |
+| Incident-event relation unavailable | authenticated `GET /v1/incidents/{id}/timeline?limit=500&cursor=...`, returning `{items, next_cursor}` with event `kind`, `ts`/`timestamp`, `actor`, `detail.event_uid`, selected `detail.summary`, `detail.priority` | Independent membership proof; never infer membership just from matching IP/time |
+| Alert lookup unavailable | authenticated `GET /v1/alerts/{event_uid}`, matching `event_uid`, tenant contract; optional incident membership fields if authoritative | Prove cited event currently exists |
+| Inventory incomplete | authenticated paginated `GET /v1/assets?limit=500&cursor=...`, returning `{items, next_cursor}` with stable asset ID, all aliases/addresses, role and criticality | Protected-target enforcement; do not claim completeness if any inventory source is unavailable |
+| Scoped read-only credential missing | issue credential authorized for the five GET routes in INTEGRATION.md; deny writes in Core auth | AI/SOAR's Core token must not mutate incidents, notifications or responses |
+| Tenant-aware deployment planned | explicit tenant ID on incidents, assets, alert detail; tenant-filter all GET routes using authenticated token; cross-tenant ID returns generic 404 | Disable temporary lab-only ACK; do not accept tenant scope from untrusted logs |
+| CryptoGuard enrichment useful | optional bounded `telemetry` list on incident detail following `contracts/incident-context.schema.json`; exclude raw logs/credentials/command lines | Investigation context, without inventing missing telemetry |
+| Identity/sensor gap | optional selected `identity_context` strings and `missing_telemetry`; optional telemetry `sensor_availability` | Unknown stays UNKNOWN |
+| Future live SOAR required | authoritative incident `data_mode=REAL/TEST/REPLAY`, plus complete protected inventory and lab designation | Unknown/test/replay must never authorize live actions |
+
+Timeline example (synthetic contract only):
+
+```json
+{
+  "items": [{
+    "kind": "event",
+    "ts": "2026-10-06T12:00:00Z",
+    "actor": "wazuh",
+    "detail": {
+      "event_uid": "EVT-example",
+      "summary": "Selected normalized evidence summary",
+      "priority": "high"
+    }
+  }],
+  "next_cursor": null
+}
+```
+
+The event must genuinely belong to the requested incident, and the token must be authorized for it. The object above is not lab evidence. Pagination may omit `next_cursor` only when the endpoint's result is complete; use `data_complete=false` for incomplete dependency-backed inventory/context so AI/SOAR fails closed.
+
