+# Known limitations — v0.29.1-sentinelzone
+
+1. **Current Core deployment not accessible.** The original package references an old Core commit. This release tests explicit legacy/normalized HTTP response contracts, not the current Windows runtime. Run the included read-only preflight, and adapt only the mapping layer if needed. BACKEND_REQUIRED_CHANGES.md lists conditional gaps, not asserted missing features.
+2. **Live PostgreSQL runtime NOT RUN.** No PostgreSQL executable/service was installed in this environment; package installation failed on environment privilege restrictions. No security restriction was changed. SQLite migrations/runtime and PostgreSQL offline SQL passed. The PostgreSQL test wrapper and CI job are supplied, but do not substitute for actually running them in a supported environment.
+3. **Docker and Windows deployment NOT RUN.** Docker/Compose is not installed here. Instructions, separate DB service and native override are supplied; no image build/start or Windows install is claimed.
+4. **Real OpenAI/local inference NOT RUN.** Only adapter request/response HTTP mocks and deterministic provider behavior were exercised. Model name is configuration; chosen models must support the requested schema format. Health checks alone do not prove inference works.
+5. **Real Shuffle/pfSense execution unavailable.** Both selectors fail closed regardless of configured credentials. Their vendor contract, target-state query, ownership-aware rollback and restoration verification must be implemented and tested before live use. Dry-run never changes a firewall or endpoint.
+6. **Frontend integration not implemented here.** Dashboard source/session architecture was not supplied and belongs to parallel work. Server-side route/identity/CSRF/secret-store requirements are documented, but no Next.js proxy was installed or browser-tested. Each human must map to a distinct AI/SOAR identity.
+7. **Trust is limited.** Citation/schema validation does not prove semantic support or model correctness. Prompt-boundary tests do not guarantee resistance of a live model to all prompt injection. Human review is required. Regex redaction cannot identify all encoded, arbitrary or unlabeled secrets; avoid unrestricted raw summaries.
+8. **One Core binding per service instance.** Local DB APIs isolate tenants. Strict tenant-aware Core responses work without lab ACK, but dynamic simultaneous per-tenant Core credentials are not implemented. Tenant-less fallback is only for explicitly acknowledged `lab`; it must not be reused for multi-tenant Core data.
+9. **Synchronous AI runs.** No distributed queue, cancellation/recovery API or auto-resume exists. Worker crashes can leave running ledger entries; a client timeout does not imply no run was created. Use the incident run list before repeating analysis.
+10. **At-most-once scope.** Durable dispatch protection is per proposal/operation and depends on retaining the database claims. It is not exactly-once vendor semantics, nor deduplication of different proposals targeting the same asset. Future adapters need effect ownership and overlap handling; restored old DB backups can lose claims.
+11. **Audit and pagination.** Audit is append-only through application APIs, not tamper-proof against the DB owner. API returns latest 200 audit entries with truncation flag; all remain persisted. Offset list pagination can shift as new records arrive. No general audit export API or retention manager is included.
+12. **Inventory/enrichment contract.** Protected-target safety depends on complete, authoritative inventory and administrator policy. Populate your real host aliases/IPs/CIDRs; none are guessed. Missing role metadata for a matched asset fails closed. Telemetry units need a confirmed upstream convention; absent sensors remain unknown and empty lists are not negative findings.
+13. **Operational safeguards remain deployment work.** Apply reverse-proxy request/time/rate controls, independent DB permissions/backups and per-user secret management. The package does not read Core DB credentials, but cannot prove external password/grant isolation. Local HTTP exception is for loopback or explicitly trusted development hosts only; production network REST uses verified HTTPS.
+14. **Dependency warning.** Locked Starlette TestClient emits an httpx integration deprecation warning. Tests pass; no warning is suppressed. The SBOM records Python packages and available licenses, not container OS image contents, CVE clearance or legal certification. Container image tags are not pinned to a verified digest in this environment.
