-# Tests
+# Testing and reproducible validation
+
+Use Python 3.12 in an isolated environment. Install the exact `requirements.lock.txt` (40 distributions). The baseline uploaded package was independently run: 97 passed. The new release extends it with contract, auth, tenant, lifecycle and failure-boundary coverage. See VALIDATION_REPORT.md for the actual run, not an assumed result.
 
 ```sh
 python -m pip install -r requirements.lock.txt
 python scripts/acceptance.py
+python -m app.cli export-contracts
+python -m pytest -q --tb=short
 ```
 
-The default suite uses a fresh file-based SQLite database per test, created by the actual Alembic migration. It tests context limits, redaction formats, log injection boundaries, valid/invalid/malformed output, unavailable providers, fabricated/wrong-incident/wrong-tenant citations, role separation, expiry, target protection, concurrent idempotency, restart claims, verification failure, rollback, YAML gate validation, REST adapter mapping, provider request envelopes, tenant isolation, and migration upgrade/downgrade/drift.
+`acceptance.py` runs pytest, Ruff, real loopback Uvicorn/SQLite smoke and both playbook simulators. It uses synthetic Core/AI and dry-run effects; it never contacts actual Core, Splunk, Wazuh, CryptoGuard, OpenAI, Shuffle or pfSense. The HTTP smoke creates a temporary DB and ephemeral loopback port, generates tokens in memory and prints no credentials. Service default runtime remains `:8004`.
+
+| Required area | Test coverage |
+| --- | --- |
+| Unit/schema/output | test_ai_output, test_context, test_migrations, test_release_contracts |
+| Authentication/roles/token boundary | test_security_health, test_approval, test_sentinelzone_contracts |
+| Cross-tenant isolation | resource/list/mutation tests and strict/legacy REST scope cases |
+| Redaction/untrusted data | test_redaction, test_prompt_injection, encoded-URL/header tests |
+| Fabricated/wrong incident/selection citation | test_evidence and REST/selected-context cases |
+| Core/provider unavailable and malformed output | test_failure_boundaries, test_ai_output, provider-construction and Core-unavailable cases |
+| Protected target/expiry/lab process | test_protected_targets, test_approval, test_playbooks, canonical-target/registration cases |
+| Duplicate/restart/uncertain execution | test_idempotency, test_failure_boundaries, timeout claim/restart cases |
+| Concurrent approval/execute/rollback | 4 competing requests per same proposal; one winning durable transition |
+| Rollback/state verification/dry-run label | test_rollback, response schemas, real-verifier receipt scope tests |
+| Migrations | SQLite roundtrip/drift/data-preserving 0001→0002; PostgreSQL offline upgrade/downgrade |
+| Dashboard schema | actual responses validated against generated JSON Schema; OpenAPI export drift |
+
+## Live PostgreSQL — opt-in and disposable only
+
+PostgreSQL runtime was NOT RUN in this environment. The dedicated live test is skipped without `TEST_DATABASE_URL`; offline dialect compilation is not reported as runtime proof.
+
+Provision a fresh database **exactly** `sentinelzone_ai_soar_test` with an independent test user, on a disposable PostgreSQL instance. Set its URL in the private process environment (not in command-line arguments or committed files), then:
+
+```sh
+python scripts/test_postgresql.py
+```
 
-For PostgreSQL, create an empty disposable database with a name ending `_test`, then set TEST_DATABASE_URL and rerun `pytest -q --tb=short`. The fixture **drops service tables between tests**. It rejects database names that do not end `_test`. Never point it at a database containing useful data. The production service database is not a test database.
+The wrapper rejects all other database names. Tests drop/recreate only that explicitly disposable AI/SOAR test schema; do not point them at production or the main Core database. The suite reruns API persistence, tenant/auth, claims, concurrency, rollback and the actual migration drift/roundtrip test using PostgreSQL. No `pytest-xdist` is supported against a single shared test DB. A CI workflow provisions PostgreSQL 16 and runs this suite, but CI execution is NOT claimed to have occurred here.
 
