@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+# Validation report — v0.29.1-sentinelzone
+
+Date: 2026-10-06. Environment: Ubuntu 24.04, CPython 3.12.14. Production requirements remain PostgreSQL; the actual runtime tests below used isolated file-based SQLite. No live Core, AI provider, firewall or endpoint credentials were supplied. No main backend or frontend source was read or modified, and no main database was contacted.
+
+**Result: ready-to-integrate release with explicit deployment gates. It is not production-verified against the current SentinelZone lab.**
+
+## Executed checks
+
+| Check | Result | Actual scope |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Uploaded input inspection | PASS | Bundle/TAR source trees byte-for-byte equal; standalone README and validation report read; input hashes in source/input-provenance.json |
+| Unmodified v0.29.0 baseline | 97 passed | Separate extracted baseline, using the supplied pinned dependency graph |
+| v0.29.1 pytest | **168 passed, 1 skipped, 0 failed** | Unit, REST mocks, schema, auth/tenant, redaction/prompt boundary/citations, policy, concurrency/restart/rollback tests |
+| Ruff | PASS | app, tests, migrations, scripts |
+| Locked dependency compatibility | PASS | All 40 exact locked Python distributions installed; uv pip check passes |
+| SQLite upgrade/downgrade/upgrade | PASS | Actual Alembic runtime, migration drift and expected tables |
+| Existing v0.29.0 data upgrade | PASS | 0002 preserves proposal/execution claim; dry-run executor bound, old live proposal marked legacy_unbound |
+| PostgreSQL SQL | PASS — OFFLINE ONLY | Upgrade and downgrade compile with PostgreSQL dialect; SQL exports in docs/ |
+| Actual Uvicorn HTTP smoke | PASS — SYNTHETIC DATA | Loopback HTTP, temporary SQLite, mock Core/provider, independent approval, simulated SUCCESS, duplicate 409, verified RESTORED |
+| Concurrent decisions/actions | PASS — SQLite | 4 competing approval, execute and rollback calls; one winning transition/claim per operation |
+| Restart/uncertain dispatch | PASS — simulator | Claim survives new app instance, crash claim and timeout; no duplicate effect; separate restoration query |
+| OpenAPI/JSON schema | PASS | Exported schemas match source; real API responses validate; required dashboard fields and UTC timestamps checked |
+| Both playbook graph simulators | PASS | Schema/order validation and WOULD EXECUTE/WOULD VERIFY labels, not external action |
+| Environment generator | PASS — Linux | lab/dev profiles, independent random DB password, no credential output, file mode 0600 and overwrite refusal |
+| Release assembly | PASS | Explicit file allowlist, ZIP/TAR, per-file/manifest SHA256 and separate archive digests; no .env, DB, cache or Git history |
+| Credential indicator check | PASS — LIMITED | Package known-token/private-key indicators, with documented synthetic test canaries; not a comprehensive secrets audit |
+| SBOM/notices | GENERATED | 40 locked distributions, package license metadata and available distribution notices; no CVE/legal/OS-image certification |
+
+The one skipped test is the live PostgreSQL migration/runtime test, explicitly skipped without `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. The suite has **71 more passing cases than the uploaded 97-test baseline**. One existing Starlette TestClient/httpx deprecation warning remains visible; it was not suppressed.
+
+`docs/acceptance-output.txt` captures the final successful acceptance output. Tests that contain “live REST” in their names use `httpx.MockTransport`; the only real HTTP server exercised is the temporary local smoke process. No report labels those mocks as real SentinelZone integration.
+
+## Not run / unavailable
+
+| Integration | Status | Reason / next gate |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Live PostgreSQL persistence, locking, migrations | **NOT RUN** | No local PostgreSQL binaries/service. Installation attempt failed on environment setuid/setgroups privilege restrictions. No restrictions bypassed. Run scripts/test_postgresql.py on a disposable sentinelzone_ai_soar_test DB. |
+| Docker image build / Compose start | **NOT RUN** | Docker/Compose unavailable. YAML and commands supplied, not runtime-verified. |
+| Windows native deployment | **NOT RUN** | This execution environment is Linux; exact Windows commands are documented. |
+| Current Core :8003 / Splunk / Wazuh / Suricata / Cowrie / CryptoGuard | **NOT RUN** | Actual service and current schema unavailable. Run authenticated read-only Core preflight with a real incident. |
+| Live OpenAI or local model inference | **NOT RUN** | No live credentials/model endpoint; provider adapters exercised with HTTP mocks. |
+| Real Shuffle / pfSense / Windows firewall | **NOT IMPLEMENTED / FAIL CLOSED** | No exact installed API/workflow contract. No dispatch occurs even if settings are populated. |
+| Real Next.js proxy/dashboard | **NOT RUN / HANDOFF PROVIDED** | Frontend belongs to parallel integration. Route, session/token/CSRF and display contracts supplied. |
+
+## Acceptance boundaries
+
+AI/SOAR stays a separate :8004 service. The only Core connector is authenticated GET REST; no Core DB URL, ORM or source import exists. Production settings enforce the dedicated database/role `sentinelzone_ai_soar`, and the installer generates new independent credentials. Creating that PostgreSQL database in the user's lab remains an installation step, not a completed remote action.
+
+AI consumes selected evidence, applies redaction before provider use and validates current citation scope. It cannot invoke SOAR. Human role separation, self-approval denial, expiry and protected systems are enforced. Dry-run has explicit flags and simulation labels. Execution/rollback claims are durable and at-most-once per proposal/operation; exactly-once external effects are not claimed. Rollback/state-verification contracts are present. Dashboard schemas, OpenAPI, integration handoff and conditional backend changes are included.
+
+No actual firewall/endpoint containment occurred. `SUCCESS` and `RESTORED` in executed tests are simulator results. Human review is required even when `trusted=true`. Live PostgreSQL and current Core validation are the main remaining environment acceptance gates; real executors remain disabled until separately implemented and verified.
