diff --git a/docs/EXECUTOR_INTEGRATION.md b/docs/EXECUTOR_INTEGRATION.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a017aa9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/EXECUTOR_INTEGRATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Future Shuffle / pfSense adapter gate
+
+Current classes: `ShuffleExecutor`, `PfSenseExecutor` in `app/soar/executors/factory.py`. Both inherit an unavailable implementation: health=unavailable, execute/verify/rollback fail closed. Configuring credentials or URLs does not enable them. Exact vendor API/version/auth/workflow contracts were not supplied and no endpoints are invented.
+
+## Administrator-only configuration
+
+| Adapter | Fields |
+| --- | --- |
+| shuffle | SHUFFLE_URL, SHUFFLE_API_KEY, SHUFFLE_WORKFLOW_ID, SHUFFLE_CA_FILE |
+| pfsense | PFSENSE_URL, PFSENSE_API_TOKEN, PFSENSE_API_CONTRACT, PFSENSE_CA_FILE |
+| common | EXECUTOR_TIMEOUT_SECONDS, SOAR_EXECUTOR |
+
+Use `ExternalExecutorConfig` as the typed config seam. Credentials are excluded from serialization. No config is taken from proposal parameters. HTTPS, internal CA and no redirects are required for a future real adapter. Fixed administrator endpoints/workflow IDs must be validated before activation.
+
+## Required implementation
+
+1. `execute(proposal)`: implement an allowlisted action, create an owned vendor effect, and return `ExecutionReceipt` (`proposal_id`, `operation=execute`, remote operation ID, `dry_run=false`, aware `accepted_at`). Receipt acceptance is not containment verification.
+2. `verify(proposal, restored=False)`: query authoritative target state independently, proving the **owned effect** on the correct target. Return `VerificationReport`: proposal/target/action, restored flag, verified flag, dry-run flag, aware `queried_at`, bounded sanitized observation and query reference. Do not use only a workflow completion or command exit code.
+3. `rollback(proposal)`: remove/restore only this proposal's owned effect and return an operation=rollback receipt. Preserve rules/process changes that existed before this action and those owned by other proposals/operators. Prevent duplicate overlapping proposals from undoing each other's containment.
+4. `verify(proposal, restored=True)`: independently query that the owned effect is removed and the original target state is restored. Absence of an API error is insufficient.
+5. Read-only reconciliation: locate remote operation/effect by stable proposal ID after crashes/timeouts, compare state and append audit without a new mutation. Stop workers for manual recovery. Never clear a durable claim to retry.
+
+Use `proposal_id + operation` as the remote idempotency key where the platform supports it. The orchestrator commits its claim first and never retries mutating dispatch. This is not exactly-once semantics. The adapter must not introduce internal HTTP mutation retries. Observe cancellation/timeouts without assuming the vendor canceled its side effect.
+
+Supply the exact installed pfSense API package/version or Shuffle workflow definition, request/response examples with credentials removed, auth mechanism, effect ownership query, rollback semantics and restored-state query before implementation. A process suspend adapter additionally needs stable process identity/start time (not only a reusable PID), process ownership and a safe resume query.
+
+## Acceptance before enabling live dispatch
+
+Test in an isolated authorized lab: independent approval, protected target at all three gates, forged/expired scope denial, execute timeout before/after effect, duplicate network delivery, restart, independent verification mismatch, rollback failure/timeout, restoration, concurrent same-target proposals, pre-existing effect preservation and credential/error redaction. No such live tests passed in this release because no live adapter is implemented.
diff --git a/docs/INTEGRATION.md b/docs/INTEGRATION.md
index dfeca66..abeb88d 100644
--- a/docs/INTEGRATION.md
+++ b/docs/INTEGRATION.md
@@ -1,53 +1,61 @@
-# Integrating the preserved SIEM backend
+# Core integration contract
 
-Inspected repository: https://github.com/ZahraAlizada5/SIEM-Backend
+AI/SOAR `:8004` owns `sentinelzone_ai_soar`. Dashboard `:3001` talks independently to Core `:8003` and to AI/SOAR through its own server-side proxy. No direct Core DB access, Core ORM import, shared DB credential or write-back API exists.
 
-Inspected commit: `0e1a1362d488979ee0f1a3552601c3a77acbb912`.
+The uploaded v0.29.0 package referenced Core commit `0e1a1362d488979ee0f1a3552601c3a77acbb912`. That is **historical input provenance**, not the current production contract. The actual Windows Core runtime/source was not available here. Compatibility is tested against explicit HTTP mocks below; run `scripts/check_core_contract.py REAL_INCIDENT_ID` against your current lab before enabling the dashboard UI.
 
-No changes were made to the downloaded reference or the remote repository. The new service is its own Git repository and release archive. No core database connection string, dashboard source, or core ORM model is used.
+## Routes and authentication
 
-## Existing REST contract
-
-| Core endpoint | Use | Mapping |
+| Method/path on Core | Adapter use | Required response |
 | --- | --- | --- |
-| GET /v1/incidents/{id} | Incident metadata | id→incident_id, title→summary, reason_codes→correlation_reasons |
-| GET /v1/incidents/{id}/timeline | Membership and selected summaries | kind=event, detail.event_uid, actor, ts, detail.summary/priority |
-| GET /v1/alerts/{event_uid} | Citation existence | Returned event_uid must exactly match |
-| GET /v1/assets?limit=500&cursor=… | Inventory and protected target checks | host_id, agent_ip, role; every page is inspected |
-| GET /health | Dependency health | ok/healthy→healthy, degraded stays degraded |
+| `GET /health` | Dependency status | object with `status: ok` or `healthy` |
+| `GET /v1/incidents/{id}` | Incident metadata and optional selected enrichment | object described below |
+| `GET /v1/incidents/{id}/timeline?limit=500&cursor=...` | Incident-event linkage and selected timeline summaries | `items` list; `next_cursor` string/null |
+| `GET /v1/alerts/{event_uid}` | Citation existence and tenant/incident scope | matching `event_uid`, tenant contract, optional `incident_id`/`incident_ids` |
+| `GET /v1/assets?limit=500&cursor=...` | Complete protected inventory and alias resolution | `items` list; `next_cursor` string/null |
+
+Every request, including health, uses `Authorization: Bearer CORE_API_TOKEN`. This must be a Core-issued read-only credential scoped to the configured tenant. The service issues GET only, uses bounded responses/timeouts, verifies TLS/optional internal CA and does not follow redirects. No fallback to legacy `/api` demo routes exists. Upstream unavailable/malformed/incomplete data fails closed; it never turns into fixture data.
 
-The older `/api` dashboard endpoints contain mock data and are deliberately not used. The existing backend's `/v1/action-proposals` skeleton remains untouched; dashboard SOAR requests must go to this service's `/v1/actions`.
+A bare object or one `{ "data": { ... } }` envelope is supported. `data_complete=false`, invalid pages, repeated cursors, page/item limits or ambiguous aliases are errors. Treat absent `next_cursor` as a completed legacy response only if the upstream actually supplies a complete list; otherwise provide explicit pagination. Do not mark a partial inventory complete.
 
-The core API has no GET asset-by-ID endpoint, so the adapter scans its paginated inventory. Pagination cycles or an exhausted page budget fail closed. For large inventories, implement a future read-only lookup endpoint and change only this adapter.
+## Mapping seam
 
-## Tenant limitation
+`app/connectors/core_backend.py` owns authenticated transport and pagination. `app/connectors/mapping.py:CoreContractMapper` owns shapes and normalization. For a different verified Core shape, adapt the mapper and its contract tests; do not import Core models or sprinkle field assumptions through AI/SOAR. `RealCoreBackendClient(..., mapper=...)` supports a custom mapper at the composition boundary.
+
+| Internal field | Accepted upstream field(s) | Missing/conflict behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| incident ID | `incident_id` or `id` | must match requested ID; conflicting aliases rejected |
+| status / priority | `status`, `priority` | required; no guessed severity conversion |
+| incident summary | `summary`, else `title` | explicit “No summary supplied” |
+| primary asset ID | `asset_id` or `host_id` | optional; conflicting aliases rejected |
+| correlation reasons | `correlation_reasons` or `reason_codes` | empty if absent; conflicting aliases rejected |
+| timeline timestamp | `timestamp` or `ts` (event may use detail `event_time`) | required for selected timeline entries |
+| timeline event | `kind=event` or `alert`, `detail.event_uid` | membership comes from this incident's endpoint |
+| original sensor | detail `original_sensor`, else `source`, else `actor` | `unknown` if absent; collector is not silently treated as original sensor when available |
+| event summary/priority | detail `summary`, `priority` | explicit missing summary; default medium selection rank only |
+| asset identity | `asset_id` or `host_id` | required |
+| asset IPs/aliases | `addresses`, `agent_ip`, `aliases`, `hostname` | all retained for protected-target checks |
+| asset protection | `role`, `criticality` | critical assets denied; matched unclassified assets fail closed |
+| lab designation | `lab_asset=true` or admin `LAB_ASSET_IDS` | absent means no process suspension |
 
